ect this fix closes)\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v2 memory: tighter PARENT wins over a looser CHILD\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v2 CPU: unlimited child does not mask a tighter parent\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v2 CPU: tighter child wins over a looser parent (the direction the pre-fix code already handled)\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v2 at the mount root itself (no nesting) still resolves correctly\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v2 'max' at every ancestor level is genuinely unlimited\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"no ancestor has cpu.max at all: UNKNOWN, not unlimited\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"a cgroup path containing '..' (path traversal) is refused outright, never resolved\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"a cgroup path that is not '/'-rooted is refused as malformed\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"a malformed /proc/self/cgroup line (missing a colon field) fails the whole file closed\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"an unreadable /proc/self/mountinfo with a readable /proc/self/cgroup falls through to v1, and v1 also unresolvable is unknown\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"v2 membership established but no v2 mount visible in mountinfo is unknown, not a silent v1 fallback\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVE