st come from the SAME ancestor level, not mixed across levels\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v1 CPU: tighter PARENT wins over a looser CHILD, aggregated across the whole paired-file chain\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v1 CPU: unlimited (-1) child does not mask a tighter parent\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v1 memory: tighter PARENT wins over a looser CHILD\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"a malformed reading at ANY ancestor level makes the whole aggregate UNKNOWN, not silently skipped\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"cgroup v1 memory sentinel is the kernel's actual LONG_MAX page-aligned value, not an approximate power of two\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"effectiveCpuCount floors a fractional nested quota but never returns zero\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"effectiveCpuCount falls back to availableParallelism only when genuinely unlimited end-to-end\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"effectiveCpuCount stays at the safe floor of 1 when nested resolution is UNKNOWN, never falls through to host core count\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"effectiveMemoryBudgetBytes resolves the real nested quota, not the (looser) mount-root reading\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {\"type\":\"test:pass\",\"details\":{\"type\":\"test\",\"name\":\"effectiveMemoryBudgetBytes falls back to a conservative fixed budget (not host total memory) when UNKNOWN\"}}\nPDPP_TEST_ACCOUNTING_EVENT {